WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:06.548
There is not a single luxury house that does not produce in India.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:10.844
We've recently had Beyonce in her tours wearing a few of our outfits. 

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:14.389
High quality. 

00:00:14.931 --> 00:00:15.682
Exclusive.

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.560
And European.

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:22.814
The hallmarks of the 180 billion euro luxury fashion industry.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.028
But unknown to many consumers is a closely guarded secret.

00:00:28.945 --> 00:00:30.697
Countries like India are often at the heart 

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.450
of what’s considered 
European luxury fashion.  

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.955
For decades, luxury fashion houses obscured their business ties

00:00:38.955 --> 00:00:41.958
to developing nations 
like India or Vietnam, 

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:45.712
where labor is cheap, and hard-to-find handicraft skills plentiful.

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:49.382
Even if you produce in Europe, 

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:54.012
at the end, the manufacturing, the reality of that business, is done in India.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:58.266
Fashion executives have long seen labels saying “Made in France” 

00:00:58.266 --> 00:00:59.559
or “Made in Italy” 

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.561
as key to higher profits.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:05.356
They worry about Western consumer stereotypes that question quality.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:07.692
There’s also the optics of sourcing goods 

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:10.236
from places where working 
conditions can be poor.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.909
But that’s increasingly contested by those fighting for transparency 

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.161
in how luxury fashion 
credits its suppliers. 

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:23.083
We set out to investigate 
what’s behind a fashion label. 

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:31.966
India’s contribution to luxury 
fashion spans empires. 

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:35.303
The nation’s embroiderers were traditionally mostly Muslim men 

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:38.932
 who had migrated to Mumbai from rural parts of the country. 

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.684
They’re known by the 
Urdu word “karigar,” 

00:01:41.684 --> 00:01:43.103
or artisan.

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:49.943
Embroidery has always been the distinction between the elite, 

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:55.698
the royal court, and the 
different layers of society.

00:01:55.698 --> 00:02:01.371
Even if a creation is done in Paris, 
even if we have ateliers in Paris 

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:04.958
doing embroidery, or in 
Italy, or in England, 

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:10.380
 India has really become the backbone of the embroidery industry. 

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:13.842
 From the 1980s, luxury brands 
have relied on India 

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.468
for much of their embroidery. 

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.813
Today, there are 
two kinds of textile facilities:

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:30.525
first, export houses in safe, well-ventilated facilities. 

00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:33.903
Second, subcontractors 
in small factories. 

00:02:38.032 --> 00:02:40.535
We're sitting in a small 
factory in central Mumbai 

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:44.330
that has completed subcontracted orders for some of the most established 

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.207
international designers.

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:50.795
When order volumes are large, Indian embroidery export houses take orders 

00:02:50.795 --> 00:02:52.797
to subcontractors throughout the city. 

00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:57.552
Sometimes they work with as many as a dozen subcontractors for a single order.

00:02:57.552 --> 00:02:59.554
This is the bottom of the supply chain, 

00:02:59.554 --> 00:03:02.265
and the working conditions 
are often the worst. 

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:04.517
Sometimes artisans, to save on rent, 

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.604
sleep on the factory floor after they've completed their work for the day.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.483
India is now one of the 
world’s largest garment exporters,

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:17.655
with a textiles and apparel market worth more than $150 billion in 2021. 

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:24.662
But the country’s connection to Western luxury brands remained secret for years.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.874
We’ve forgotten the past.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.584
We’ve forgotten the excellence of craft.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:32.962
The big question in fact is to 
know why these luxury brands

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:37.675
are so hesitant in putting 
“Made in India” on these products, 

00:03:37.675 --> 00:03:42.096
when they should be, by law, 
putting in “Made in India.”

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.439
The global fashion system 
is built on exploitation. 

00:03:54.442 --> 00:03:58.905
It's not coincidence, but by design, that most of fashion today is produced

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:02.033
in regions where freedom 
of association is restricted, 

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:05.662
where it's difficult for workers 
to exert their rights.

00:04:06.871 --> 00:04:09.290
So when it comes to 
obscuring supply chains,

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.127
there's a myth that being transparent is commercially sensitive, 

00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:16.839
 that it would harm business to be transparent and disclose 

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:19.425
who and where your clothes are made. 

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:22.929
Improved transparency is absolutely essential to protecting the people 

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:25.473
who make our clothes, who are often some of the most vulnerable people

00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:26.766
in global supply chains. 

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:32.814
Our investigation looked at 
one jacket as a case study. 

00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:37.193
The garment, embellished entirely with delicate micro-mirrors, 

00:04:37.193 --> 00:04:40.530
retails for almost 43,000 Euros 
(about $45,000).

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:44.033
And according to exporters in Mumbai, it took more than 2,000 hours 

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.285
to embroider in India.

00:04:46.327 --> 00:04:50.039
Seamstresses estimated the piece then underwent less than 100 hours 

00:04:50.039 --> 00:04:52.208
of stitching and finishing 
touches in Europe. 

00:04:53.376 --> 00:04:57.880
It carries a “Made in France” tag, reflecting European Union regulations 

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.092
that define the country of origin as the place where the last substantial transformation took place — not where the bulk of labor was completed.

00:05:01.092 --> 00:05:04.971
transformation took place, not where the bulk of labor was completed.

00:05:06.097 --> 00:05:09.600
A Dior spokesperson told Bloomberg that even though the mirrored coat is  

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.730
 an exceptional piece that showcases India’s “savoir-faire,”

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:16.065
nevertheless “it was made in France, 

00:05:16.065 --> 00:05:18.526
which justifies the dedicated 
‘Made in’ label.” 

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:24.282
Still, in March 2023, Dior became one of the first international luxury brands

00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:26.784
to showcase a collection in India 

00:05:26.784 --> 00:05:30.330
saying it’s determined to promote the country’s artisanal legacy worldwide.

00:05:30.788 --> 00:05:34.334
Chanakya International, the Indian export house that embroidered clothing 

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.669
for the Dior Mumbai collection, 
declined to comment.

00:05:37.337 --> 00:05:41.466
What we are very happy about 
and elated about is that

00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:45.345
actually Dior took a first step to announce its supplier. 

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:48.139
We were all kept hidden for a long time.

00:05:50.475 --> 00:05:53.436
It has changed the way 
the others are thinking

00:05:53.436 --> 00:05:56.856
putting us more forward 
for recognition of our work 

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.900
and our embroidery 
and our craftsmanship

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:02.862
which earlier they wanted to show maybe that it was done in Paris or Italy. 

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:08.159
Now they are happy to say that this is made, this embroidery is done in India.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:11.245
India’s growing importance 
across industries

00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:15.291
has made the world’s most populous nation impossible to ignore.

00:06:15.291 --> 00:06:18.336
One recipient of this attention 
is Gayatri Khanna.

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:23.925
Her company, Milaaya Embroideries, has climbed atop the ranks of Mumbai’s 

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:26.386
highest-profile export houses. 

00:06:26.636 --> 00:06:30.723
She counts Versace, Balmain 
and Dolce &amp; Gabbana 

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.016
as just some of her clients.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.561
Today we are a 450-employee business.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:38.106
We are in the center 
in the heart of Mumbai. 

00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:41.109
We have over 150-odd clients, 

00:06:41.109 --> 00:06:45.988
which are amazing and 
we cherish all our collaborations.

00:06:57.792 --> 00:07:01.504
When you talk about “Made In India” you tend to celebrate 

00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:02.922
craft which is coming from India,

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:04.424
at the same time 
you are also celebrating 

00:07:04.424 --> 00:07:06.050
 the people who are making it.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:09.804
I think it is also all about 
how to dream together.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:14.392
For many in the industry, 
the “Made in India” garment tag

00:07:14.392 --> 00:07:18.479
is paving the way for a younger, progressive wing of creatives, 

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:22.817
who want more fairness and transparency in how luxury fashion

00:07:22.817 --> 00:07:24.694
credits its suppliers.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:31.617
So today I feel that things are slightly changing. Slowly changing. 

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.744
Because they cannot lie anymore. 

00:07:33.744 --> 00:07:37.915
They have to acknowledge that in the last 30 years, they have been 

00:07:37.915 --> 00:07:41.502
manufacturing in the country, manufacturing in India.

